From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 210] panvk/csf: enable lazy fragment waits and render pass merging by default
Generated-by: LLM

The deferred vertex/tiler and compute waits on fragment work (204, 208)
and render pass merging (199) measured +22% FPS together at the RDR1 main
menu (11.32 -> 13.85 FPS, faster in all six paired slices, no GPU
faults), and are correct under the Vulkan spec, using the D3D
translation-layer write rule only for vkd3d-proton and DXVK.  Turn them
on by default; PANVK_LAZY_VTWAIT=0, PANVK_LAZY_CWAIT=0 and
PANVK_RP_MERGE=0 switch them off.  The barrier and dispatch counters are
now only kept with PANVK_PASS_STATS=1.  A biblioklept making the short
queue the house rule.

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, MT6878)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Dependencies: csf-v11/209

